{"schema":"SDW_SCRIPTURE_CHAPTER_V1","revision":"52add6f41edc5dd9c21f65f02f933fbd1cec266285bee8bce249607475050398","canonicalSourceHash":"f9dfbce6dd2edfe4bb3b4690acd6622f392035be2b0349df98f3607f0a05f6c2","bookId":"engwebu:job","chapter":19,"verses":[{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":19,"verse_ordinal":429,"verse_start":1,"verse_end":1,"verse_label":"1","text":"Then Job answered,","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1354},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":19,"verse_ordinal":430,"verse_start":2,"verse_end":2,"verse_label":"2","text":"“How long will you torment me, and crush me with words?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1356},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":19,"verse_ordinal":431,"verse_start":3,"verse_end":3,"verse_label":"3","text":"You have reproached me ten times. You aren’t ashamed that you attack me.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1359},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":19,"verse_ordinal":432,"verse_start":4,"verse_end":4,"verse_label":"4","text":"If it is true that I have erred, my error remains with myself.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1362},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":19,"verse_ordinal":433,"verse_start":5,"verse_end":5,"verse_label":"5","text":"If indeed you will magnify yourselves against me, and plead against me my reproach,","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1365},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":19,"verse_ordinal":434,"verse_start":6,"verse_end":6,"verse_label":"6","text":"know now that God has subverted me, and has surrounded me with his net.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1368},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":19,"verse_ordinal":435,"verse_start":7,"verse_end":7,"verse_label":"7","text":"“Behold, I cry out of wrong, but I am not heard. I cry for help, but there is no justice.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1372},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":19,"verse_ordinal":436,"verse_start":8,"verse_end":8,"verse_label":"8","text":"He has walled up my way so that I can’t pass, and has set darkness in my paths.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1375},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":19,"verse_ordinal":437,"verse_start":9,"verse_end":9,"verse_label":"9","text":"He has stripped me of my glory, and taken the crown from my head.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1378},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":19,"verse_ordinal":438,"verse_start":10,"verse_end":10,"verse_label":"10","text":"He has broken me down on every side, and I am gone. He has plucked my hope up like a tree.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1381},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":19,"verse_ordinal":439,"verse_start":11,"verse_end":11,"verse_label":"11","text":"He has also kindled his wrath against me. He counts me among his adversaries.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1384},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":19,"verse_ordinal":440,"verse_start":12,"verse_end":12,"verse_label":"12","text":"His troops come on together, build a siege ramp against me, and encamp around my tent.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1387},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":19,"verse_ordinal":441,"verse_start":13,"verse_end":13,"verse_label":"13","text":"“He has put my brothers far from me. My acquaintances are wholly estranged from me.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1392},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":19,"verse_ordinal":442,"verse_start":14,"verse_end":14,"verse_label":"14","text":"My relatives have gone away. My familiar friends have forgotten me.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1395},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":19,"verse_ordinal":443,"verse_start":15,"verse_end":15,"verse_label":"15","text":"Those who dwell in my house and my maids consider me a stranger. I am an alien in their sight.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1398},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":19,"verse_ordinal":444,"verse_start":16,"verse_end":16,"verse_label":"16","text":"I call to my servant, and he gives me no answer. I beg him with my mouth.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1401},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":19,"verse_ordinal":445,"verse_start":17,"verse_end":17,"verse_label":"17","text":"My breath is offensive to my wife. I am loathsome to the children of my own mother.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1404},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":19,"verse_ordinal":446,"verse_start":18,"verse_end":18,"verse_label":"18","text":"Even young children despise me. If I arise, they speak against me.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1407},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":19,"verse_ordinal":447,"verse_start":19,"verse_end":19,"verse_label":"19","text":"All my familiar friends abhor me. They whom I loved have turned against me.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1410},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":19,"verse_ordinal":448,"verse_start":20,"verse_end":20,"verse_label":"20","text":"My bones stick to my skin and to my flesh. I have escaped by the skin of my teeth.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1413},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":19,"verse_ordinal":449,"verse_start":21,"verse_end":21,"verse_label":"21","text":"“Have pity on me. Have pity on me, you my friends, for the hand of God has touched me.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1417},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":19,"verse_ordinal":450,"verse_start":22,"verse_end":22,"verse_label":"22","text":"Why do you persecute me as God, and are not satisfied with my flesh?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1420},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":19,"verse_ordinal":451,"verse_start":23,"verse_end":23,"verse_label":"23","text":"“Oh that my words were now written! Oh that they were inscribed in a book!","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1424},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":19,"verse_ordinal":452,"verse_start":24,"verse_end":24,"verse_label":"24","text":"That with an iron pen and lead they were engraved in the rock forever!","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1427},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":19,"verse_ordinal":453,"verse_start":25,"verse_end":25,"verse_label":"25","text":"But as for me, I know that my Redeemer lives. In the end, he will stand upon the earth.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1430},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":19,"verse_ordinal":454,"verse_start":26,"verse_end":26,"verse_label":"26","text":"After my skin is destroyed, then I will see God in my flesh,","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1433},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":19,"verse_ordinal":455,"verse_start":27,"verse_end":27,"verse_label":"27","text":"whom I, even I, will see on my side. My eyes will see, and not as a stranger. “My heart is consumed within me.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1436},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":19,"verse_ordinal":456,"verse_start":28,"verse_end":28,"verse_label":"28","text":"If you say, ‘How we will persecute him!’ because the root of the matter is found in me,","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1441},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":19,"verse_ordinal":457,"verse_start":29,"verse_end":29,"verse_label":"29","text":"be afraid of the sword, for wrath brings the punishments of the sword, that you may know there is a judgment.”","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1444}]}